{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880130",
      "title": "Replacing \"methods\" with Regular Functions",
      "lectureOrder": 291,
      "videoOrder": 258,
      "sourceHash": "44505c59a9b344234051cf1e301d961d57f62d76f7faffa0811484355222c40a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.15,
          "end": 5.27,
          "en": "So we had to look at ref for single values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.27,
          "end": 10.07,
          "en": "and reactive for objects if we wanna group values together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.07,
          "end": 12.96,
          "en": "and want to ensure that we can edit properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 16.293,
          "en": "just like this, and still maintain reactivity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.4,
          "end": 19.73,
          "en": "Now, enough about ref and reactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.73,
          "end": 21.65,
          "en": "We're going to see more of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.65,
          "end": 25.49,
          "en": "as we write more code with the Composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.49,
          "end": 29.25,
          "en": "But now let's actually come back to this simple slide here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.25,
          "end": 33.81,
          "en": "We learned that the data that's managed with the data option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.81,
          "end": 37.38,
          "en": "can be replaced with ref and reactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 39.86,
          "en": "Now we also have methods computed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.86,
          "end": 42.46,
          "en": "and watch which I mentioned would be replaced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.46,
          "end": 45.81,
          "en": "So Let's now move on to methods here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.81,
          "end": 50.27,
          "en": "For that, let's say, we have a button here on this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.27,
          "end": 53.74,
          "en": "and it will be a simple button with no particular styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.74,
          "end": 56.11,
          "en": "And there I'll say change age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.11,
          "end": 60.4,
          "en": "And when we click it, I wanna change my age here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.4,
          "end": 63.4,
          "en": "So for that, of course, we can add a click listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.4,
          "end": 67.28,
          "en": "And now, normally with the Options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.28,
          "end": 69.76,
          "en": "we would point at a method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.76,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "We would add our methods option, to this config object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.93,
          "end": 78.53999999999999,
          "en": "and then have something like set new age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 80.02,
          "en": "or any name like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.02,
          "end": 85.02,
          "en": "And if we then had, age data property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.52,
          "end": 86.96000000000001,
          "en": "like 31, initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.96000000000001,
          "end": 91.63,
          "en": "we would set this age equal to 32, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.63,
          "end": 94.3,
          "en": "that is how we would do it with the Options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.3,
          "end": 96.843,
          "en": "with data and methods combined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 100.55,
          "en": "Now we're using the Composition API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.55,
          "end": 102.45,
          "en": "and therefore we don't have data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 104.34,
          "en": "and we won't have methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.34,
          "end": 107.61,
          "en": "But how can we then, call a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "call some code to be executed, when an event occurs?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.08,
          "end": 114.243,
          "en": "How do we bind click here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.21000000000001,
          "end": 116.92099999999999,
          "en": "Well, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.92099999999999,
          "end": 120.13,
          "en": "we could access user age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.13,
          "end": 122.18,
          "en": "and set a new value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.18,
          "end": 125.32,
          "en": "You might remember that simple JavaScript expressions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.32,
          "end": 129.12,
          "en": "like this, are allowed, and therefore we could do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.12,
          "end": 132.94,
          "en": "So if I keep this code, and actually remove this timer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.94,
          "end": 136.41,
          "en": "because I no longer wanna update name and age with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.41,
          "end": 138.14,
          "en": "so let's remove the timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.14,
          "end": 139.793,
          "en": "So if I save that now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.97,
          "end": 143.61,
          "en": "we have the button, and it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.61,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "But running all the code that should run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 149.18,
          "en": "upon button clicks and form submissions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.18,
          "end": 150.73,
          "en": "in the template like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.73,
          "end": 153.73,
          "en": "is definitely not what we wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.73,
          "end": 156.87,
          "en": "It's a good practice to not put too much logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.87,
          "end": 157.91,
          "en": "into the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.91,
          "end": 161.12,
          "en": "And if you consider more complex examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.12,
          "end": 162.75,
          "en": "like form submissions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.75,
          "end": 165.51,
          "en": "where you also wanna validate user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.51,
          "end": 167.71,
          "en": "and maybe show alerts and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.71,
          "end": 170.383,
          "en": "then this absolutely would not be an option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.6,
          "end": 174.37,
          "en": "Instead, the solution is actually very simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.37,
          "end": 178.62,
          "en": "though it might look strange when you see it the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 179.98,
          "en": "The setup method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.98,
          "end": 183.94,
          "en": "is called when Vue sets up this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.94,
          "end": 186.16,
          "en": "It's called only once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.16,
          "end": 189.96,
          "en": "And in this setup method, you basically define the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.96,
          "end": 192.62,
          "en": "which should be available in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.62,
          "end": 195.85,
          "en": "Well, you cannot just define your data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.85,
          "end": 197.9,
          "en": "you can also define the functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.9,
          "end": 200.073,
          "en": "that should be available to your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.92000000000002,
          "end": 202.47,
          "en": "We can add a function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.47,
          "end": 204.84,
          "en": "set new data could be the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.84,
          "end": 207.653,
          "en": "and we can expose that to the template as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.52,
          "end": 211.292,
          "en": "It might look strange that we define a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.292,
          "end": 212.68,
          "en": "(indistinct) of a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.68,
          "end": 215.28,
          "en": "but this is regular JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.28,
          "end": 218.7,
          "en": "We can create functions inside of functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.7,
          "end": 220.78,
          "en": "This is absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 220.78,
          "end": 223.69,
          "en": "And actually, we've set timeout before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.69,
          "end": 225.22,
          "en": "we did nothing different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.22,
          "end": 227.59,
          "en": "There we also had a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.59,
          "end": 229.79,
          "en": "which we created on the fly here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.79,
          "end": 231.69,
          "en": "that's also just a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.69,
          "end": 233.74,
          "en": "to find (indistinct) of the setup method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.95,
          "end": 237.49,
          "en": "So defining a function here is fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.49,
          "end": 241.593,
          "en": "and then this function, we could set user age equal to 32.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.49,
          "end": 246.26,
          "en": "And now the question is, how do we expose this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.26,
          "end": 249.513,
          "en": "to the template so that we can bind it to this click event?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 250.77,
          "end": 253.33,
          "en": "Well, just as we expose data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.33,
          "end": 255.81,
          "en": "we can add a new key value pair,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 259.59,
          "en": "to this object which we return here in the setup method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 259.59,
          "end": 262.13,
          "en": "and, for example, have a set H key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.13,
          "end": 265.03,
          "en": "and point at set new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 265.03,
          "end": 269.963,
          "en": "Or set new age maybe, and change the name up here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.44,
          "end": 273.83,
          "en": "And I'm not executing the function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.83,
          "end": 275.17,
          "en": "I'm just pointing at it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.17,
          "end": 278.74,
          "en": "So I'm storing a pointer at this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 278.74,
          "end": 283.11,
          "en": "in the set age property in this returned object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.11,
          "end": 284.67,
          "en": "And this returned object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 284.67,
          "end": 289.4,
          "en": "simply holds all the things you can use in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 289.4,
          "end": 292.40999999999997,
          "en": "That may be data, like our user object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 292.40999999999997,
          "end": 295.073,
          "en": "but it may also be a pointer at a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.15,
          "end": 298.37,
          "en": "So now we'll set H as the key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.37,
          "end": 303.263,
          "en": "so therefore, we can bind, or click event here to set age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.63,
          "end": 308.49,
          "en": "And this will then trigger, the set new age function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 308.49,
          "end": 310.673,
          "en": "at which we point in set age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 311.65,
          "end": 315.02,
          "en": "And therefore if I save that, and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 315.02,
          "end": 317.3,
          "en": "we can still change the age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 317.3,
          "end": 319.74,
          "en": "but now with this exposed function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 319.74,
          "end": 321.02,
          "en": "And that's really simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 321.02,
          "end": 324.56,
          "en": "but this is how you expose functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 324.56,
          "end": 326.86,
          "en": "which you typically bind to click events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 326.86,
          "end": 330.13,
          "en": "but which you also can execute, just like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 330.13,
          "end": 332.9,
          "en": "between interpolation for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.9,
          "end": 336.33,
          "en": "That's how you expose them to your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 336.33,
          "end": 340.01,
          "en": "You define them in setup and return them in your object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 340.01,
          "end": 342.71,
          "en": "And that's your replacement for methods in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 342.71,
          "end": 344.67,
          "en": "simple as that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 344.67,
          "end": 348.25,
          "en": "And of course, it does not just work with a reactive object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 348.25,
          "end": 351.81,
          "en": "but instead if we would go back to using refs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 351.81,
          "end": 353.76,
          "en": "so if I reverse this all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 353.76,
          "end": 356.24,
          "en": "and I go back to U name and U age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 356.24,
          "end": 359.18,
          "en": "and having two refs instead of one object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 359.18,
          "end": 364.18,
          "en": "then of course we can also update our data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 364.2,
          "end": 367.713,
          "en": "With U age value equal to 33 for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 368.6,
          "end": 370.45,
          "en": "Now we just need to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 370.45,
          "end": 372.129,
          "en": "the code we exposed to the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 372.129,
          "end": 375.99,
          "en": "because I went back to using two individual values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 375.99,
          "end": 377.58,
          "en": "So now we could again expose,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 377.58,
          "end": 381.003,
          "en": "let's say a username and a age, like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 382.47,
          "end": 386,
          "en": "Exposing these two refs, which are defined here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 386,
          "end": 387.71,
          "en": "where one of them has changed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 387.71,
          "end": 389.45,
          "en": "through the value property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 389.45,
          "end": 391.51,
          "en": "which is watched by Vue as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 391.51,
          "end": 394.37,
          "en": "And then in the template, we can use username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 394.37,
          "end": 397.22,
          "en": "and age to output both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 397.22,
          "end": 399.34000000000003,
          "en": "So username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 399.34000000000003,
          "end": 401.173,
          "en": "and age here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 402.35,
          "end": 403.90999999999997,
